# NanoClaw environment overrides. Copy values into .env (which is gitignored).
# This file documents non-obvious flags; it is not exhaustive.

# Direct-to-provider Gmail/Calendar (per-group), bypassing the OneCLI gateway.
# When "true", any MCP server that declares NO_PROXY in its env has its proxy
# vars blanked at spawn, so it reaches Google directly with the GROUP'S OWN
# credentials. Without this, the OneCLI gateway substitutes its connected
# (business) Google account on Gmail calls — i.e. a personal-assistant group
# (Ayah) silently reads the wrong mailbox.
#
# REQUIRED for Ayah's personal Gmail. If Ayah's Gmail suddenly reverts to the
# business account, this flag is the first thing to check — and the host log
# says so explicitly:
#   ACTIVE  -> "Gateway bypass ACTIVE (direct-to-provider...)"
#   BROKEN  -> "Gateway bypass OFF: ... USE_CUSTOM_GMAIL is not \"true\""
#   grep:   grep -E "Gateway bypass" logs/nanoclaw*.log
# See docs/UPDATES.md for the full write-up.
USE_CUSTOM_GMAIL=true
